ca.loc.gov/lccn/sn83030313/1866-05-28/ed-1/seq-8/"}, {"mark": "¶", "claim": "Arrived Queenstown (15 May)", "citation": "Hubbard & Winter, North Atlantic Mail Sailings 1840-75 (USPCS, 1988; rev. 2014), p. 210", "source_kind": "compiled", "displayable": false, "crop": null, "verbatim": null, "lineage_id": "hw:inman-220-067-e:1", "source": "hw"}, {"mark": "7", "claim": "Arrived Queenstown (at 10 p.m. to-day)", "citation": "The Express (London), 16 May 1866, “MEXICO”, HMD item art0076 (Heritage Made Digital, British Library)", "source_kind": "newspaper", "displayable": false, "crop": null, "verbatim": null, "lineage_id": "hmd:L5f8970db89988dfa", "source": "hmd", "url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.15056046"}, {"mark": "8", "claim": "Spoken / sighted lat 45 57, lon 41 47 (1866-05-03)", "citation": "New York Herald, 8 May 1866, p. 8, col. 4", "source_kind": "newspaper", "displayable": true, "crop": "https://tile.loc.gov/image-services/iiif/service:ndnp:dlc:batch_dlc_goldenglow_ver01:data:sn83030313:00271743543:1866050801:1146/3013,2313,965,220/640,/0/default.jpg", "verbatim": "The steamship China at Halifax reports had fine weather.\nOn April 30, lat 51, lon 13[?], passed the Hecla, bound west;\nMay 2, lat 48 35, lon 33 55[?], saw (supposed) steamer Atlanta,\nbound west; 3d, lat 46 23, lon 40 51, spoke bark Gibraltar (Br);\nlat 45 57, lon 41 47, spoke City of London (not the steamer),\nbound east; 5th, lat 43 20, lon 54 35, spoke ship Maroborough,\nbound west.", "lineage_id": "herald:L5e5220ef3b4692e9", "source": "herald", "url": "https://chroniclingamerica.loc.gov/lccn/sn83030313/1866-05-08/ed-1/seq-8/"}, {"mark": "9", "claim": "Spoken / sighted lat 41 16, lon 65[?] 14 (May 7)", "citation": "New York Herald, 11 May 1866, p. 9, col. 4", "source_kind": "newspaper", "displayable": true, "crop": "https://tile.loc.gov/image-services/iiif/service:ndnp:dlc:batch_dlc_goldenglow_ver01:data:sn83030313:00271743543:1866051101:1183/2812,244,959,343/640,/0/default.jpg", "verbatim": "Steamship City of London, from New York for Liverpool,\nMay 7, lat 41 16, lon 65[?] 14.", "lineage_id": "herald:Lff7f19baabf7cc59", "source": "herald", "url": "https://chroniclingamerica.loc.gov/lccn/sn83030313/1866-05-11/ed-1/seq-9/"}, {"mark": "10", "claim": "Spoken / sighted 41 N 66 W (7th)", "citation": "Lloyd's List, 19 May 1866, p. 3, col. 1 (British Newspaper Archive)", "source_kind": "newspaper", "displayable": false, "crop": null, "verbatim": null, "lineage_id": "lloyds:L1b8fe084ba0ca3d0", "source": "lloyds", "url": null}, {"mark": "11", "claim": "Spoken / sighted 44 N 46 W (10th)", "citation": "Lloyd's List, 19 May 1866, p. 3, col. 1 (British Newspaper Archive)", "source_kind": "newspaper", "displayable": false, "crop": null, "verbatim": null, "lineage_id": "lloyds:L2892f472b2692b27", "source": "lloyds", "url": null}, {"mark": "12", "claim": "Brought news Queenstown (05-15) news to 1866-05-05", "citation": "The Express (London), 16 May 1866, “MEXICO”, HMD item art0076 (Heritage Made Digital, British Library)", "source_kind": "newspaper", "displayable": false, "crop": null, "verbatim": null, "lineage_id": "hmd:L3f4eb78263d06609", "source": "hmd", "url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.15056046"}, {"mark": "13", "claim": "In port Liverpool (17th)", "citation": "New York Herald, 30 May 1866, p. 5, col. 6", "source_kind": "newspaper", "displayable": true, "crop": "https://tile.loc.gov/image-services/iiif/service:ndnp:dlc:batch_dlc_goldenglow_ver01:data:sn83030313:00271743543:1866053001:1371/4512,6907,989,329/640,/0/default.jpg", "verbatim": "17th, City of London,\nMirehouse, do;", "lineage_id": "herald:Lb8374e0f49d8b15a", "source": "herald", "url": "https://chroniclingamerica.loc.gov/lccn/sn83030313/1866-05-30/ed-1/seq-5/"}, {"mark": "14", "claim": "Cleared New York (1866-05-04)", "citation": "New York Herald, 5 May 1866, p. 8, col. 5", "source_kind": "newspaper", "displayable": true, "crop": "https://tile.loc.gov/image-services/iiif/service:ndnp:dlc:batch_dlc_goldenglow_ver01:data:sn83030313:00271743543:1866050501:1116/3909,2209,959,120/640,/0/default.jpg", "verbatim": "Steamship City of London (Br), Mirehouse, Queenstown\nand Liverpool—J G Dale.", "lineage_id": "herald:Lcc71f50178e8b83a", "source": "herald", "url": "https://chroniclingamerica.loc.gov/lccn/sn83030313/1866-05-05/ed-1/seq-8/"}, {"mark": "15", "claim": "Cleared New York (1866-05-04)", "citation": "The Sun (New York), 5 May 1866, p. 4, col. 3", "source_kind": "newspaper", "displayable": true, "crop": "https://tile.loc.gov/image-services/iiif/service:ndnp:nn:batch_nn_brown_ver01:data:sn83030272:0020653607A:1866050501:0432/1377,2293,709,325/640,/0/default.jpg", "verbatim": "City of\nLondon, Liverpool", "lineage_id": "sun:Lfb3caecc9d1b6e16", "source": "sun", "url": "https://chroniclingamerica.loc.gov/lccn/sn83030272/1866-05-05/ed-1/seq-4/"}, {"mark": "16", "claim": "Cleared New York (1866-05-04)", "citation": "New-York Tribune, 5 May 1866, p. 7, col. 2", "source_kind": "newspaper", "displayable": true, "crop": "https://tile.loc.gov/image-services/iiif/service:ndnp:dlc:batch_dlc_delphi_ver03:data:sn83030214:00206530832:1866050501:0045/1026,2085,1060,120/640,/0/default.jpg", "verbatim": "Steamship City of London (Br.), Mirehouse, Liverpool, John G.\nDale.", "lineage_id": "tribune:Lac62c65302414f4e", "source": "tribune", "url": "https://chroniclingamerica.loc.gov/lccn/sn83030214/1866-05-05/ed-1/seq-7/"}, {"mark": "17", "claim": "Specie $311,000", "citation": "New York Herald, 6 May 1866, p. 4, col. 1", "url": "https://chroniclingamerica.loc.gov/lccn/sn83030313/1866-05-06/ed-1/seq-4/", "source_kind": "newspaper", "displayable": true, "crop": "https://tile.loc.gov/image-services/iiif/service:ndnp:dlc:batch_dlc_goldenglow_ver01:data:sn83030313:00271743543:1866050601:1120/132,3806,993,366/640,/0/default.jpg", "verbatim": "There was a larger\nexport of treasure than usual to Europe by this day's\nsteamers, the total aggregating $991,515, of which\nabout $600,000 was in bar gold and silver. The Her-\nmann took of this amount $221,300, the Allemania\n$63,000, the City of London $311,000, the Malta $250,615\nand the Lafayette $145,600. The export for the week\nhas been $1,247,240.", "lineage_id": "herald:L632aa9620cf31e90", "source": "herald"}], "aboard": {"specie": [{"text": "311,600 dol. and 2,000l. sterling", "marks": ["7"]}, {"text": "$311,000", "marks": ["17"]}], "passengers": [{"n": 413, "marks": ["7"]}], "mails": [], "headlines": [], "mail": []}}